  "status_text": "A simple rule can make as few mistakes as any circuit under the same gate limit. Ask whether any of the chosen switches are on. Lean checked this for groups of copied switches, with the light required off when every switch is off (L-lib-1351). Each gate reads at most two wires. Read whole banks of copies and at most one partial bank, then combine them using OR. The same minimum applies with AND and NOT gates available. A companion check ties group coverage to allowed misses when timing also has to be exact (L-lib-1346).",
